    LOAD-TIME, measured on CPU:
      expansion, index -> flat             20401.1 us  ( 67.21 MiB)
      VBO upload, unique vertices only      3733.2 us  ( 41.02 MiB)
      ratio expansion/upload                  5.46x

    PER-FRAME, volume only - cost is BLOCKED, no GL context:
      no glDrawElements, expanded            67.21 MiB per draw
      VBO + index buffer, resident once      52.22 MiB total
      per-frame volume ratio                  1.29x
      corner sends, expanded               2936559 per draw
      unique vertices, indexed             1792108 uploaded once

    The per-frame advantage of VBO/VAO is real and follows
    from the absent imports, but its COST is driver, bus and
    per-vertex call overhead: BLOCKED here. See DEC-008.

Run twice and compare the medians; a shift of more than a few
percent on the same machine means something changed.
